llama_set_embeddings on a context without pooling did not re-reserve the graph,
but toggling embeddings reorders its leafs (t_embd is expanded first).
ggml_gallocr_needs_realloc compares node counts/sizes and the leaf count, not
the leaf order, so the stale leaf table was reused and a leaf such as out_ids
got buffer_id -1 -> segfault in ggml_gallocr_alloc_graph (Soprano TTS, b11804).

--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -1339,8 +1339,10 @@
 void llama_context::set_embeddings(bool value) {
     LLAMA_LOG_DEBUG("%s: value = %d\n", __func__, value);
 
-    // a pooled context computes the logits only without embeddings, so the toggle changes the graph shape
-    if (cparams.embeddings != value && cparams.pooling_type != LLAMA_POOLING_TYPE_NONE) {
+    // a pooled context computes the logits only without embeddings, so the toggle changes the graph shape;
+    // without pooling it still reorders the graph's leafs (t_embd is expanded first), which ggml-alloc's
+    // realloc check does not compare, so the stale leaf allocations would be reused
+    if (cparams.embeddings != value) {
         sched_need_reserve = true;
     }
 
